    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d781">

                <pb facs="0810" n="802" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg802"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221/1505: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Then in France, to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Jean de Luz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-02-28T13:00:00+00:00">February 28, 1939—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>586. Marquis de Rialp has finally informed me that he is ready to deliver the 81
                    American prisoners at the frontier as soon as the Loyalists agree to an
                    exchange. The situation of the Spanish Government is such just now as to make
                    this difficult of realization but I am asking Del Vayo in Paris to transmit the
                    proposition to Negrin.<anchor n="74" xml:id="d781-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d781-f1" n="74" xml:id="d781-f1-content">
                <p>Spanish Prime Minister.</p>
            </note>
